definition:
    Chinese-American experimental physicist (1912–1997), called the 'First Lady of Physics'. During the Manhattan Project she improved gaseous-diffusion uranium enrichment. Her crowning achievement came in 1956: the Wu experiment confirmed that mirror symmetry (parity) is violated in beta decay — a discovery so fundamental it won Tsung-Dao Lee and Chen-Ning Yang the 1957 Nobel Prize while Wu herself was overlooked.
